    },
    {
      "name": "MyPendingCircleInvites",
      "context": {
        "mode": "all",
        "context": "Circle"
      },
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "invite",
          "object": "CircleInvite",
          "scope": "allAvailableContexts"
        }
      ],
      "sort": [
        {
          "field": "SentAt",
          "direction": "asc"
        }
      ],
      "comment": "The home feed's counterpart for invites: every circle a caller has access\nto via `pendingCircleInvite` (declared above) is one they have been\ninvited to but not yet joined, so `SCOPE allAvailableContexts` here\nreaches exactly the invites addressed to them across every circle --\nwithout needing a circle already selected, unlike `CONTEXT REQUIRED`.\n\nThis deliberately does not join `Circle` to project a `CircleName`: a\n`CONTEXT_GRANT` only ever puts the *granted* object (`CircleInvite`) in\nreach of the object-scope gate for its target, never the context's own\nroot object (`Circle`). `CirclePolicy` has no rule that would let a\npending invitee read the `Circle` record itself -- `ROLE CircleMember`\ndoes not apply (they are not one yet) and no policy vocabulary here\nexpresses \"may read because a grant admits me to this context\" the way\n`CONTEXT_MEMBER` expresses relationship access on a different object's\nfield. Joining it anyway would silently drop every row for exactly the\ncaller this read model exists for, the same shape of finding as\n`learnings/implementation/reference-app-models.md`'s \"a cross-band\noverlay cannot name which band\".",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "InviteeEmail",
          "source": "invite",
          "field": "InviteeEmail"
        },
        {
          "name": "Status",
          "source": "invite",
          "field": "Status"
        },
        {
          "name": "SentAt",
          "source": "invite",
          "field": "SentAt"
        },
        {
          "name": "Invitee",
          "source": "invite",
          "field": "Invitee",
          "comment": "Not shown -- projected only so `MyPendingInvites` (`ui.adlj`) can gate its\nAccept/Decline row actions to the row's actual invitee. `allowAuthenticated\nSearchInvites` (above) is unconditioned, and `allowCircleOwnerReadInvites`\nlegitimately lets an owner read every invite their own circle has sent --\nso this read model also surfaces a circle owner's own outgoing invites,\nnot only invites addressed to the caller. Both commands' own `REQUIRE\nInvitee == runtime.userId` step guard makes offering the buttons on\nsomeone else's invite safe either way, but showing a button that always\nfails for its own caller is still worth avoiding."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "CircleMemberRoster",
      "comment": "Projects the membership row's own `User` lookup rather than joining the\n`User` object as a second source.\n\nIt used to source `User` with `SCOPE all` and project `user.Email`, which\nmade the circle overview a per-circle directory of email addresses. It also\nmade the roster depend on a whole-record read grant on `User`, which\n`UserPolicy` no longer gives an ordinary caller. `FIELD Member FROM\nmember.User` inherits that field's `LOOKUP User DISPLAY DisplayName`\n(Phase 91), so the row carries the member's id in `values` and their\ndisplay name in `display` -- exactly what Giggle Band's\n`BandMemberAvailability.Member` already does, resolved through the same\nfield-scoped label read.",
      "context": {
        "mode": "required",
        "context": "Circle"
      },
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "member",
          "object": "CircleMember",
          "scope": "currentContext"
        }
      ],
      "sort": [
        {
          "field": "Role",
          "direction": "asc"
        }
      ],
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "Member",
          "source": "member",
          "field": "User"
        },
        {
          "name": "Role",
          "source": "member",
          "field": "Role"
        },
        {
          "name": "JoinedAt",
          "source": "member",
          "field": "JoinedAt"
        }
      ]
    },
