    {
      "name": "UserPolicy",
      "object": "User",
      "comment": "A signed-in caller may resolve a collaborator's *display name*, and nothing\nelse -- in particular not their email address.\n\n`FIELDS DisplayName` is what makes that true rather than aspirational: a\nrule that names `FIELDS` cannot match a whole-record request at all\n(`ruleMatches`, `policy-engine.ts`), so this grants the display field and\nnever the record it lives on. `Email` and `Timezone` have no rule of their\nown, so default deny applies to them, and there is deliberately no `SEARCH`\nrule -- search is the enumeration primitive over a user directory, and once\n`CircleMemberRoster` stopped sourcing `User` nothing legitimate needed it.\n`UserSystemAdminPolicy` above keeps `SystemAdmin`'s whole-record access\nuntouched.\n\n`DISPLAY` moved from `Email` to `DisplayName` in the same change, and had\nto: while `Email` was the display field, \"the display field only\" would\nhave granted exactly the thing this policy exists to withhold. Every\n`LOOKUP User` in this app now displays `DisplayName` for the same reason.\n\nThis narrows the whole-object `ALLOW SEARCH/READ AUTHENTICATED` pair that\nstood here while registration was invite-only -- every authenticated caller\nhad been vouched for by somebody already inside. Phase 99 adds self-service\nregistration, so \"anyone who can reach the authority may sign up\" plus \"any\nauthenticated caller may read every `User` record\" would have been an open\ndirectory of every user's name and email.\n\nWhat must not come back is `ROLE CircleMember`, which would match nothing:\na context-scoped `ROLE` condition only resolves against an object that is\nitself scoped to that context (`SCOPE Circle FIELD Circle`, as\n`Event`/`Note`/... declare) or is itself a context's own bound object\n(`Circle`, for `CONTEXT Circle OBJECT Circle`). `User` is neither, so\n`getPolicyRequestContextTargets` (`context-scope.ts`) can only ever resolve\ntargets against the `User` context -- the caller's own identity selection.\nThe compiler refuses that shape now\n(`ADL_POLICY_ROLE_PRINCIPAL_UNREACHABLE`, Phase 93).\n\nTwo narrower grants remain inexpressible and are not attempted here. \"Only\npeople I share a circle with\" needs `CONTEXT_MEMBER` to key on a field\nholding the record's own id, and a `User` record has none. \"My own record\nin full\" needs the same thing: `OWNER` matches\n`meta.createdBy`/`CreatedBy`/`OwnerId`, none of which a `User` record\ncarries about itself, and no policy condition can compare a record's id to\n`runtime.userId`.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "name": "allowAuthenticatedReadUserDisplayName",
          "effect": "allow",
          "principal": {
            "match": "authenticated",
            "roles": [],
            "groupRoles": [],
            "users": [],
            "owner": false
          },
          "action": "read",
          "state": [],
          "fields": [
            "DisplayName"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "CirclePolicy",
      "object": "Circle",
      "rules": [
        {
          "name": "allowCircleMemberSearchCircles",
          "effect": "allow",
          "principal": {
